# Common Design Pitfalls

| Pitfall | Impact |
|---|---|
| No Automated Device Enrollment | Shared iPad is unavailable |
| No supervision | Shared iPad cannot be properly enabled |
| User affinity enabled | Shared iPad configuration may fail or not behave as expected |
| No federation | Users may need separate Managed Apple IDs |
| Using user-assigned apps | Apps may not function correctly in shared scenarios |
| Insufficient storage | User sessions may be evicted |
| Confusing Shared iPad with Shared Device Mode | Wrong architecture selected |

